data: {"type":"response.completed","sequence_number":1256,"safety_buffering":false,"response":{"id":"resp_0aa8b4f023358add016acb0bbf9b7c8194ab61c145d71ef8cc","object":"response","created_at":1791691711,"completed_at":1791691733,"status":"completed","background":false,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"presence_penalty":0.0,"moderation":null,"model":"gpt-6.1-sol","access_programs":{"cyber":"standard"},"previous_response_id":null,"instructions":"You are an expert coding assistant operating inside pi, a coding agent harness. You help users by reading files, executing commands, editing code, and writing new files.\n\n<tools>\n- read: Read file contents\n- bash: Execute bash commands (ls, grep, find, etc.)\n- edit: Make precise file edits with exact text replacement, including multiple disjoint edits in one call\n- write: Create or overwrite files\n\nIn addition to the tools above, you may have access to other custom tools depending on the project.\n</tools>\n\n<rules>\n- Use bash for file operations like ls, rg, find\n- Use read to examine files instead of cat or sed.\n- You can inspect PI_* environment variables for current model and session details.\n- Use edit for precise changes (edits[].oldText must match exactly)\n- When changing multiple separate locations in one file, use one edit call with multiple entries in edits[] instead of multiple edit calls\n- Each edits[].oldText is matched against the original file, not after earlier edits are applied. Do not emit overlapping or nested edits. Merge nearby changes into one edit.\n- Keep edits[].oldText as small as possible while still being unique in the file. Do not pad with large unchanged regions.\n- Use write only for new files or complete rewrites.\n- Be concise in your responses\n- Show file paths clearly when working with files\n</rules>\n\n<docs>\nPi documentation (read only when the user asks about pi itself, its SDK, extensions, themes, skills, or TUI):\n- Main documentation: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/README.md\n- Additional docs: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs\n- Examples: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/examples (extensions, custom tools, SDK)\n- When reading pi docs or examples, resolve docs/... under Additional docs and examples/... under Examples, not the current working directory\n- When asked about: extensions (docs/extensions.md, examples/extensions/), themes (docs/themes.md), skills (docs/skills.md), prompt templates (docs/prompt-templates.md), TUI components (docs/tui.md), keybindings (docs/keybindings.md), SDK integrations (docs/sdk.md), custom providers (docs/custom-provider.md), adding models (docs/models.md), pi packages (docs/packages.md), environment variables (docs/environment-variables.md), MCP servers (docs/mcp.md), codemode scripts and non-LLM models such as classifiers and image models (docs/codemode.md)\n- When working on pi topics, read the docs and examples, and follow .md cross-references before implementing\n- Always read pi .md files completely and follow links to related docs (e.g., tui.md for TUI API details)\n</docs>\n\n<addendum>\nKeep changes focused and readable. Use clear names and avoid needless duplication. Verify the changed behavior with appropriate checks before submitting.\n</addendum>\n\n<cwd>\n/home/agent/work\n</cwd>","output":[{"type":"reasoning","id":"rs_0aa8b4f023358add016acb0bc0bf7c81949a9bbb2280474590","summary":[{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Evaluating implementation strategies**\n\nI'm thinking about my time budget and how to implement these edits through a generated transformations script. The rules require precision. It seems tough to replace hidden content with a unique function block using bash. Instead, I wonder if replacing entire project pages is necessary. Maybe defining a hidden filter for repeated pairs could help. Ideally, I'd replace unique entries without impacting the overall page structure, focusing on distinct hidden pairs without confusion."}],"content":[],"encrypted_content":"gAAAAABqywvHNG_AMvcapVQUQPHUaffimug3rwDQPN7jIV7MfkD2pxX_vVH99G3VhhFAYJ-K_iq4H7EyA2Fwbs8hT5JdwagdqdHTRKEXTyXi7eguOPFjR9LIOOMzRprfgThpp95thCurk4xf63rjNpjtjdjLymFke4UlDm70-0Tx8EUrPgi7B3vn79hXyeVXOhkSlhzDyBPXbhc4wqu_6WBZu66Wv4IcEbGkQUaav4G9WWCKDzIsKyLwvBuniLB2fQPiLFKmmuysIEtTqc-zsmjzZrwhf1y-5-fBLvHg7IcCs5t5vS0U0O49JfqAuffEP5_1_IzCYWMFgSyDcVH2a8PnkO0OWXmcUS7taN2gyuoORyFA52bdlhCO8Innw6arZ5Tfn3QSXJeWa-M1LHQuujBBqvmZzt9mepXLvSSVsn3Ob8zI-1ixLA5epLcEiWKn5WFvZjema9tvw3_exydjciydx-DNE086tVNyyUcP6I_o6YpqTfhl0LTikcKHHR-FBO-Rb6ZKins3VBmR8vWgVndyCZ4hVmXt6E6bjZpUAOlrU1ZiNXdbMs83XDapp238KU2m_BciJRKaXQWSkH4HbQwuwX0YTwLvovhYRiKDLwsFBcaA48Lf5epns5OOMNlvQTRaGJtB-t44boWcOB6seewzQyxfoF6VRclnZcq6IZ5X0yrugflJYjqR5RxSQxFxlb-6cgI-Rv8_ytfwEmrKseUTWipx52q9srj9apr5iIFtpdPwG8h-tbbVEcNn5HXmut4Ht9C46yGtqKHAPmABd9Bzwajstc0ixAxg3oH2kgyfydroYpFncsPyZl0u8N3L2hWE6fm9mRt1sykTX928L9URPrUyS96kbRAtEA52SZ5-SIbR7o5Q776weYoZ_tF4sJWUIOf38UaHqY7ZMw5wJvs4WbJ7png8cyKCHZa-7sH5zRFHysUWjHiHFlFSC1tLJrDemIi_Hbdw7d0pznteaaY0Wj8r7cGZbUMQyzF8QjZkNbuOYFsYtIzF0GMpKU34Pso689u8zEoTIu4p_rRb-cLWTcGsqAdFomJC6t-EnO8WE2n_Pd_QInJXLH-JtzYj5Zcn5oFjzlxno_75Q2dqE2DA8DdesY_TVriz9FiGQlpt1NJiduHqMbv_Yr0CXgimdACKhcrIIQ4AJv7fxKaY88wbGdI_WveIP-FD16z6iju42A73sQ1IzqK8ynUqsRTSDDh-bMMdgkkNPGAvGgMgkSdIOTFWq6TflnJrnnNgD2ivdg5_OKOYpHsi18O0wXwpVXhyAm7qxpURB9slOZs201En1_MLR4beJKNlfdH6Fhz3fM4VHf78swIEzkyK0Lcm8vjof0wyxT8UkP2eoWA3jFKhFtHgFn10A-gCm93m2gGAJ9qfIIEGel2DjNM2xjDRqtGfZ_jM26Z0u_WtWGw_kZdmPRtxCPYkE7AEItw4g9PDkmyxMvuBbgffnQu5uVr4E08yOmrQ7muXY1P1Ql9-6wMp7f4qJe2Bho0vf_SYpKyTsKInYArEzol7hIppRv6kHp-c80Eu7RW7tPROtdHlZYNHUbGP2CCx0w1g_IiUufLBVgv3X1bHiBndsyhJ4zTjSK4vJ-SWL_cR_siMLa37rhmfRKojX4p414-qkfYFABoMqKgPbcO8lmBPQLNneyShDgDMu44aa3Gr4V4HdHXu2PiGI9XxRkCdAiR8GoNBB9OblhaJNFAFoIS9TlfH8Jr6e_ygwM519rBLNvJx9I5R95yjQ1U8V4h0prt5JdrW2Ah5uQWr0ac-lau4N0AHNwueW_VYSjUywlZjePELmRkZ93oBgeZyWcmLrmhwv-yAF8Fo4QUnWBDGzf28k8yBosCo3MY2rs0diQZTnq7oBt-xK3OlIGp4Rrf4